{
  "core_message": "Sully Sullenberger saved all 155 passengers by ditching his plane into the Hudson River in under four minutes.",
  "mood": "tense",
  "title": "155 Lives Saved in 4 Minutes: The Hudson Miracle",
  "description": "In January 2009, a flock of birds sent an Airbus A320 out of the sky. The pilots had less than four minutes to decide where to land, and they chose the river.\n\nThis is the story of the Miracle on the Hudson, where every single person on board survived a high-speed water landing.\n\nKey points:\n- Bird strike caused dual engine failure\n- 155 passengers and crew survived\n- Entire event took less than 4 minutes\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"US Airways Flight 1549\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/US_Airways_Flight_1549), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nA tour of four great rivers; the Hudson, Mohawk, Susquehanna and Delaware in 1769; being the journal of Richard Smith of Burlington, New Jersey; (1906) (14580460149).jpg (Internet Archive Book Images, No restrictions): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_tour_of_four_great_rivers;_the_Hudson,_Mohawk,_Susquehanna_and_Delaware_in_1769;_being_the_journal_of_Richard_Smith_of_Burlington,_New_Jersey;_(1906)_(14580460149).jpg\n2025 Hudson River plane crash rescue efforts.png (oakpale, CC BY 2.5): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2025_Hudson_River_plane_crash_rescue_efforts.png\nSteamboats on Hudson River at Highlands.jpg (Currier and Ives, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steamboats_on_Hudson_River_at_Highlands.jpg\nA tour of four great rivers; the Hudson, Mohawk, Susquehanna and Delaware in 1769; being the journal of Richard Smith of Burlington, New Jersey; (1906) (14580460149).jpg (Internet Archive Book Images, No restrictions): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_tour_of_four_great_rivers;_the_Hudson,_Mohawk,_Susquehanna_and_Delaware_in_1769;_being_the_journal_of_Richard_Smith_of_Burlington,_New_Jersey;_(1906)_(14580460149).jpg\nU.S. Coast Guard Rescue Swimmer Demonstration in Hudson River DVIDS1092530.jpg (U.S. Coast Guard Auxiliary photo/Auxiliarist Hope Wright, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:U.S._Coast_Guard_Rescue_Swimmer_Demonstration_in_Hudson_River_DVIDS1092530.jpg\nRobert Havell, Jr. - Hudson River North to Croton Point, 1851.jpg (Robert Havell, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Havell,_Jr._-_Hudson_River_North_to_Croton_Point,_1851.jpg\nForcing the Hudson River Passage, October 9 1776- 1951 69.jpeg (William Joy / After Dominic Serres, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Forcing_the_Hudson_River_Passage,_October_9_1776-_1951_69.jpeg\n\n3D models:\nAirbus A320 by Andre11230 (CC BY 4.0) https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/none-790a19f65d5646539ed975c96fedb313",
